---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Private & Browser-Based | ConvertAnyFile" description="Edit images locally in your browser with privacy-first tools. Remove visible watermarks with batch, shape, and text masks, or use the focused Gemini AI Logo Remover for Circle and 4-Point-Star editing.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Useful image edits without an upload queue.</h1><p>Focused browser-side tools for common image tasks. Both live watermark tools share one local batch editor, while each product exposes only the mask choices that fit its job.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Available now</span><h2>Two focused watermark workflows on one editing engine.</h2><p>Remove Watermark is the flexible general editor: Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, 4-Point Star, and Text masks. Gemini AI Logo Remover is intentionally simpler, with only Circle and 4-Point Star. Both support smart shared-or-individual batch editing, local repair, Before/After preview, output controls, cancellation, and ZIP download.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Smart batch behavior</span><h2>Same layout? Start fast. Mixed layouts? Keep masks independent.</h2><p>When uploaded images share an aspect ratio, the editor starts with One mask for all. When mixed aspect ratios are detected, Edit individually is selected automatically. The recommendation is never a lock: you can switch the toggle whenever your images need a different workflow.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Image decoding, mask editing, visible-pixel repair, output encoding, and ZIP creation happen in your browser. There is no source-image upload step or AI inference API.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Choose the right tool</span><h2>General watermark or focused Gemini-style badge?</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best when</th><th>Mask choices</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/remove-watermark/"><strong>Remove Watermark</strong></a></td><td>The visible mark can be rectangular, round, square, diamond-shaped, sparkle-shaped, or text.</td><td>Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, 4-Point Star, Text</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini AI Logo Remover</strong></a></td><td>You want a fast, focused workflow for a small visible Gemini-style corner badge.</td><td>Circle, 4-Point Star</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Separate from converters</span><h2>Interactive editing stays separate from format conversion.</h2><p>Converters use the existing EngineAdapter batch pipeline. Image Tools use a stateful canvas editor for masks, move/resize interaction, per-image overrides, previews, and destructive visual edits. They still share navigation, privacy principles, output infrastructure, responsive design, and SEO foundations.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>No empty tool pages</strong><p>Only working Image Tools receive public routes. Planned resize, compress, crop, rotate, blur, object-removal, and background-removal ideas stay visible on the roadmap until their engines are implemented and validated.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
